  {
   "id": "control/history-bytes",
   "category": "host-limit",
   "retired": true,
   "retired_reason": "This row asserted `HostLimit HistoryBytes [0,65531) provenance=host-replay-preflight`, a host replay-preflight bound of the 44329dc design. CALC-STATE-02's selected committed-session route runs every line directly on the committed session and restores it on failure, so no host history or replay bound exists and this refusal cannot fire. The surviving host bound is the 65,536-byte input frame, exercised by control/transport-limit, and the design's post-format output assertion is a defensive infrastructure failure with no reachable input. The row is retired rather than re-pointed at a guest category: a guest `ResourceLimit` would no longer be a host-bound control."
  },
  {
   "id": "control/replay-work",
   "category": "host-limit",
   "retired": true,
   "retired_reason": "This row asserted `HostLimit ReplayWork [0,65401) provenance=host-replay-preflight`, the second 44329dc replay-preflight bound. It is retired for the same reason as control/history-bytes: the committed-session route removed replay, so the bound no longer exists and the row would otherwise assert a refusal the design cannot produce. The host-failure controls that remain are control/transport-limit, control/host-timeout, control/memory-cap and control/worker-killed, none of which may print a `ResourceLimit`."
  },
